# Domain 6: the Hyperpax application trades against the perpetuals and spot precompiles and reads the gateway data services.

[feature.6]
name = "application"
scope = "The Hyperpax application resolves every chain call through one precompile address table (perpetuals 0x1015, price feed 0x1020, spot 0x1021-0x1025), encodes with ABIs generated from the contract files, carries price bound, deadline, time in force, reduce-only and take-profit and stop-loss on every perpetuals write, uses six-decimal USDL amounts and exact approvals, holds one USDL cross-margin account, trades spot on the spot precompile set, reads one gateway over REST, WebSocket with snapshot resume and GraphQL with its existing operation set, signs through the embedded wallet with a PKCE session, classifies precompile custom errors and completes the trading round trip against a local node at v6.12.0."
requirements = ["6001", "6002", "6003", "6004", "6005", "6006", "6007", "6008", "6009", "6010", "6011", "6012", "6013", "6014", "6015", "6016", "6017", "6018", "6019"]
completion_task = "6.3.99"

[req.6001]
title = "Every chain call of the application resolves through one precompile address table"
ac_1 = "The address module src/core/network/precompiles.ts (planned) exports the perpetuals precompile 0x1015, the spot set 0x1021 to 0x1025 and the oracle precompile 0x1020 as 20-byte viem addresses, and DIAMOND_ADDRESS (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:10-11) is removed."
ac_2 = "Each address keeps the environment override of envAddress (Hyperpax:src/core/spot/addresses.ts:23-27) and a value that is not a 20-byte hex address is refused at module load."
ac_3 = "PECOR_CONTRACTS (Hyperpax:src/core/spot/addresses.ts:31-60) reads PECOR, PECORQuoter, PECOROrders, PECORStopOrders and PECORVault from the address module, PriceOracle resolves to 0x1020 and TransactionTracker (Hyperpax:src/core/spot/addresses.ts:52-55) is removed."
ac_4 = "USDL is one address: the perpetuals collateral entry (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:75-79) and the spot USDL entry (Hyperpax:src/core/spot/addresses.ts:146-153) both read the six-decimal USDL token of contracts/libraries/Constants.sol:14-16, which after the upgrade is the native pointer of uusdl at the same address; the PAX entry is the native pointer of uhpx and the SID entry the native pointer of usid (contracts/spot.md), and no WPAX9 address remains in the address module."
ac_5 = "No source file under src/ names the Diamond address or a PECOR contract address other than through the address module."
ac_6 = "The chain stays chain id 125 from paxeerChain (Hyperpax:src/core/chain.ts:16-17)."

[req.6002]
title = "The precompile ABIs are generated from the contract files and typed end to end"
ac_1 = "src/core/network/abi/PerpsPrecompile.ts (planned) is generated from contracts/perps.md in the as-const shape of Hyperpax:src/core/network/abi/PositionFacet.ts:1-2 and contains every method of the perpetual call-site table, the TimeInForce enumeration, every event and every custom error of contracts/perps.md."
ac_2 = "The barrel Hyperpax:src/core/network/abi/index.ts:1-27 exports the perpetuals precompile ABI, and no hook imports PositionFacetABI, OrderBookFacetABI, QuoterFacetABI, TradingAccountABI or VaultFactoryFacetABI."
ac_3 = "The spot ABI files keep every selector the application encodes, for example marketBuy (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:313) and placeLimitBuy (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOROrders.ts:526); a selector that differs from contracts/spot.md fails the golden test."
ac_4 = "The call builders pass typed ABIs, so the params as any cast of readContract (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useContract.ts:8-16) never carries a precompile call and a signature drift fails pnpm tsc --noEmit."

[req.6003]
title = "Position calls go to the perpetuals precompile with their price bound and deadline"
ac_1 = "openPosition (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePosition.ts:63-64) targets 0x1015 with marketId, collateralToken, collateralAmount, leverage and isLong plus acceptablePrice, deadline, takeProfitPrice and stopLossPrice."
ac_2 = "addSize (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePosition.ts:121-122) targets 0x1015 with positionId, additionalCollateral in USDL base units, leverage at 18 decimals, acceptablePrice and deadline."
ac_3 = "closePosition (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePosition.ts:79-80) targets 0x1015 with positionId, acceptablePrice from quoteClosePosition exitPrice and deadline."
ac_4 = "partialClose (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePosition.ts:89-90) targets 0x1015 with positionId, closeSizeUsd at 18 decimals, acceptablePrice from quotePartialClose and deadline, and the positions panel offers it beside handleClose (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsPositionsPanel.tsx:857-876)."
ac_5 = "addCollateral and removeCollateral (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePosition.ts:100-101, :110-111) target 0x1015 with the amount in USDL base units."
ac_6 = "getPosition, getUserPositionIds and getOpenInterest (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePosition.ts:29-30, :38-39, :47-48) read 0x1015."
ac_7 = "getPositionCollateralToken reads the collateral token by its output name instead of output index 5 (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePosition.ts:69-73)."

[req.6004]
title = "Order calls go to the perpetuals precompile with time in force, reduce-only and attached TP/SL"
ac_1 = "placeLimitOrder (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerpsOrders.ts:36-40) targets 0x1015 with marketId, isLong, triggerPrice, sizeUsd, leverage, collateralToken, collateralAmount plus timeInForce, reduceOnly, takeProfitPrice and stopLossPrice."
ac_2 = "placeStopLimitOrder (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerpsOrders.ts:58-59) targets 0x1015 with limitPrice and the same four added fields."
ac_3 = "placeTakeProfitOrder and placeStopLossOrder (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerpsOrders.ts:81-82, :91-92) target 0x1015 with positionId and an 18-decimal trigger price."
ac_4 = "cancelOrder (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerpsOrders.ts:71-72) targets 0x1015 and the positions panel cancel (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsPositionsPanel.tsx:885) uses it."
ac_5 = "getOrder and getUserOrderIds (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerpsOrders.ts:10-11, :19-20) read 0x1015."

[req.6005]
title = "Quotes come from the perpetuals precompile and the gateway"
ac_1 = "quoteMarket (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useQuoter.ts:116-122) reads 0x1015 only after the gateway ticker read (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useQuoter.ts:82) fails."
ac_2 = "The fallback's fixed maintenanceMarginBps (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useQuoter.ts:109) is replaced by the value the precompile returns."
ac_3 = "quoteOpenPosition and quoteClosePosition (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useQuoter.ts:126-140, :142-150) read 0x1015 and their entryPrice and exitPrice outputs (Hyperpax:src/core/network/abi/QuoterFacet.ts:163, :11) feed the price bound."
ac_4 = "quotePartialClose (Hyperpax:src/core/network/abi/QuoterFacet.ts:239) is called before partialClose and its exitPrice feeds the bound."

[req.6006]
title = "Collateral is a USDL cross-margin account held by the perpetuals precompile"
ac_1 = "deposit and withdraw (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useVault.ts:44-62) target 0x1015 instead of a per-user vault through src/hooks/perps/useAccount.ts (planned), and useVault.ts with getVaultAddress and createVault (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useVault.ts:8-24) is removed."
ac_2 = "getBalance and getLockedBalance (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useVault.ts:26-42 and the multicall at Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePortfolioStats.ts:154-155) read the account at 0x1015 for the connected address."
ac_3 = "topUpPosition and transferMargin (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useMarginMode.ts:147-211) target 0x1015 with USDL base-unit amounts."
ac_4 = "getAccountSummary and getPositionMargin (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useMarginMode.ts:96-145, :213-264) read 0x1015."
ac_5 = "Margin mode is cross: useMarginMode and useSetMarginMode (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useMarginMode.ts:15-94) are removed, MARGIN_MODE_LABELS (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:286-289) shows the cross label and the toggle (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsPositionsPanel.tsx:1008) is removed."
ac_6 = "useEmergencyWithdraw (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useMarginMode.ts:266-297) is removed and withdrawal of the available balance uses withdraw."
ac_7 = "COLLATERAL_TOKENS and COLLATERAL_OPTIONS (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:64-87) list USDL only."

[req.6007]
title = "Every on-chain amount uses the decimals of its unit"
ac_1 = "AdjustCollateralModal converts add-collateral, remove-collateral and add-size collateral with six decimals instead of parseEther (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/modals/AdjustCollateralModal.tsx:68, :81, :86) and keeps leverage at 18 decimals."
ac_2 = "TopUpPositionModal (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/modals/TopUpPositionModal.tsx:39) and TransferMarginModal (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/modals/TransferMarginModal.tsx:46) convert with six decimals."
ac_3 = "DepositWithdrawModal converts with safeParseUnits (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/amounts.ts:26-38) instead of BigInt(Math.floor(num * 10 ** decimals)) (Hyperpax:src/app/modals/DepositWithdrawModal.tsx:198)."
ac_4 = "getCollateralDecimals throws for an unknown token instead of returning 18 (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/amounts.ts:40-45)."
ac_5 = "Prices, sizeUsd and leverage stay at 18 decimals as the form converts them (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:327-348), with sub-1x leverage refused."
ac_6 = "The spot stable decimals come from the market's quote token metadata instead of the fixed decimalsStable = 6 (Hyperpax:src/widgets/spot/SpotOrderForm.tsx:418)."

[req.6008]
title = "Approvals request exactly the amount of the call they precede"
ac_1 = "ensureAllowance treats an allowance at or above the amount as sufficient and the MAX_UINT256 / 2 threshold (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotApprovals.ts:40, :139) is removed."
ac_2 = "A short allowance is raised through approveExact (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotApprovals.ts:87-100) for exactly the amount, never approveMax (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotApprovals.ts:67-79, :143)."
ac_3 = "The perpetuals allowance helper replacing ensureDiamondAllowance (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePosition.ts:13-22) uses spender 0x1015."
ac_4 = "The spot rails approve 0x1021 for market orders, 0x1022 for limit orders and 0x1023 for stop orders (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotOrders.ts:151-156, :288-293)."
ac_5 = "No approval requested by the application exceeds the amount of its call."

[req.6009]
title = "Time in force and order options reach the precompile or are removed"
ac_1 = "The perpetuals form maps ioc, fok and postOnly (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:291-293) to timeInForce IOC, FOK and PostOnly, and none of them to GTC."
ac_2 = "IOC, FOK and post-only are mutually exclusive: post-only clears IOC and FOK, which already exclude each other (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:1084-1085)."
ac_3 = "reduceOnly (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:290) is sent as reduceOnly on limit and stop-limit orders."
ac_4 = "The hidden toggle (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:295, :1088) is removed and orderConfirm (:294) opens a confirmation step before signing."
ac_5 = "A spot limit order with IOC or FOK (Hyperpax:src/widgets/spot/SpotOrderForm.tsx:421-427) takes its minimum output from the limit price through expectedOutFromPrice (Hyperpax:src/core/spot/slippage.ts:160), so a buy never pays above its limit."
ac_6 = "Spot post-only keeps forcing GTC (Hyperpax:src/widgets/spot/SpotOrderForm.tsx:367) and the spot reduce-only toggle (Hyperpax:src/widgets/spot/SpotOrderForm.tsx:207, :816) is removed."

[req.6010]
title = "Take-profit and stop-loss entered in the form are carried to the precompile"
ac_1 = "With tpslEnabled (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:234) the market branch sends tpPrice and slPrice (:235-236) as takeProfitPrice and stopLossPrice in openPosition, which the call at :482 omits today."
ac_2 = "The limit and stop-limit branches (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:486, :490) send the same two fields; an unset price is 0."
ac_3 = "A long requires stopLossPrice below the reference price below takeProfitPrice and a short the mirror; a failing pair blocks submit with TRADE_TP_SL_INVALID (Hyperpax:src/core/errors/classify.ts:251-253)."
ac_4 = "SetTpSlModal keeps placeTakeProfitOrder and placeStopLossOrder for an open position at 18 decimals (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/modals/SetTpSlModal.tsx:84-91)."
ac_5 = "A position opened with TP and SL reads back with both prices attached."

[req.6011]
title = "Every market-priced perpetuals write carries a price bound and a deadline"
ac_1 = "acceptablePrice for a market open is entryPrice * (10000 + bps) / 10000 for a long and entryPrice * (10000 - bps) / 10000 for a short with bps = DEFAULT_SLIPPAGE_BPS (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:354)."
ac_2 = "Close and partial-close bounds use the quoted exitPrice with the opposite rounding."
ac_3 = "deadline is the reference block timestamp plus DEFAULT_MARKET_DEADLINE_SECONDS (Hyperpax:src/core/spot/slippage.ts:27) built with buildDeadline (:75)."
ac_4 = "An aged quote (QUOTE_MAX_AGE_MS, Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:178) is re-fetched and the bound recomputed instead of blocking submit."
ac_5 = "Every bound is a bigint at 18 decimals computed with integer arithmetic only."

[req.6012]
title = "The order form submits through one pure order plan"
ac_1 = "src/core/perps/orderPlan.ts (planned) returns the ordered call list for market, limit, stop-limit and scaled orders and handleSubmit (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:444-506) submits exactly that list."
ac_2 = "A scaled order reads scaledStartPrice, scaledEndPrice, scaledTotalOrders and scaledDistribution (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:227-231) and returns N placeLimitOrder calls at evenly spaced prices from start to end inclusive."
ac_3 = "Ascending and descending distributions weight rung i by i+1 and N-i and the integer remainder goes to the last rung."
ac_4 = "The custom distribution (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsOrderForm.tsx:29) has no input and returns no calls; fewer than 2 or more than 20 rungs return no calls."
ac_5 = "After a successful submit the form clears the inputs and the chart order lines together."

[req.6013]
title = "The spot widgets trade on the spot precompile set"
ac_1 = "marketBuy and marketSell (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotOrders.ts:163-168, :253-258) target 0x1021 with their argument lists unchanged."
ac_2 = "placeLimitBuy, placeLimitSell, cancelLimitOrder, modifyLimitOrder, getUserLimitOrders and getLimitOrder (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotOrders.ts:280-381) target 0x1022."
ac_3 = "placeStopLimitBuy, placeStopLimitSell, cancelStopLimitOrder, placeStopLoss, cancelStopLossOrder and the four stop readers (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotOrders.ts:402-571) target 0x1023."
ac_4 = "Every quoter read (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotQuoter.ts:141-286) targets 0x1024 and the 23-field QuoteResult parse is unchanged."
ac_5 = "The WPAX9 wrap before a sell (Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotOrders.ts:223-227) is removed because the PAX native pointer serves no deposit(): a native sell passes the PAX pointer address and the spot precompile moves bank uhpx directly (contracts/spot.md); the spot deadline semantics (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/meta-ag/engine/PECOR.sol:132-135) are unchanged."
ac_6 = "The spot route gate (Hyperpax:src/pages/spot.tsx:2-3) asserted by Hyperpax:tests/audit-regressions.test.ts:7-11 stays as tested."

[req.6014]
title = "The data hooks read one gateway over REST"
ac_1 = "INDEXER_BASE_URL and REST_API_URL (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:23-25, :33) derive from NEXT_PUBLIC_PERPS_GATEWAY_URL and the orderbook, open-interest and ticker routes (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/Orderbook.tsx:148, Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useQuoter.ts:54, :82) keep their paths."
ac_2 = "SPOT_API_BASE (Hyperpax:src/core/spot/api.ts:14-16) derives from the gateway and the user routes (Hyperpax:src/core/spot/api.ts:283-361) keep their paths."
ac_3 = "PERFDB_URL (Hyperpax:src/core/perfdb/client.ts:12-14) derives from the gateway and the auth routes (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerfdbAuth.ts:168, :175, :201) keep their paths."
ac_4 = "The chart candle feed keeps FEED_ORIGIN and candleFeedUrl (Hyperpax:src/core/feeds.ts:2, :8-14)."
ac_5 = "No REST base constant names a host literal other than through the gateway variable."

[req.6015]
title = "WebSocket streams resume from a snapshot with sequence checks"
ac_1 = "The perpetual order book subscribes with {event: \"subscribe\", topic: \"<SYMBOL>@perp_orderbook\"} instead of the action/channel frame (Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/Orderbook.tsx:231-235)."
ac_2 = "Every stream passes frames through sequenceGuard (Hyperpax:src/core/net/realtime.ts:29-47) and a snapshot frame resets the per-topic baseline."
ac_3 = "A gap (seq greater than last + 1) closes the socket with code 4000 as at Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useSidPaxMarketStream.ts:294, fetches the REST snapshot, resubscribes and drops deltas at or below the snapshot seq."
ac_4 = "A changed snapshotId drops local state for every topic of that socket and resubscribes (Hyperpax:data_api.md:70-82)."
ac_5 = "Reconnect uses scheduleActive and the retry-after and 1013 handling of watchSocket (Hyperpax:src/core/net/realtime.ts:8-22, :84-85)."
ac_6 = "All socket URLs (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:34-36, Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useMarketsStream.ts:29, Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useSidPaxMarketStream.ts:70, Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotMarketStream.ts:34, Hyperpax:src/hooks/chain/useExplorerStream.ts:29, Hyperpax:src/hooks/spot/useSpotUserStream.ts:32-34) derive from the gateway and every symbol shares one socket."

[req.6016]
title = "GraphQL reads keep the application's operation set on the gateway"
ac_1 = "INDEXER_GRAPHQL (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:47-50) points at the gateway GraphQL endpoint and its graphql-transport-ws path, and the client keeps POST queries and the subprotocol (Hyperpax:src/core/graphql/client.ts:92-93, :336, :347, :366)."
ac_2 = "The 51 query operations of Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useSubgraph.ts:23-528 keep their names, variables and selections."
ac_3 = "The seven subscription operations (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useIndexerSubscriptions.ts:79-259, Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePortfolioStats.ts:177, Hyperpax:src/widgets/trading/PerpsPositionsPanel.tsx:798) keep their names and root fields."
ac_4 = "The PerfDB operations (Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerfdbUser.ts:17, Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerfdbBalances.ts:18, Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/useDailyPnl.ts:16, Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerfdbTraderStats.ts:21, Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerfdbAlerts.ts:37, Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerfdbReferrals.ts:57, :75, Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerfdbCompetitions.ts:64, :79, Hyperpax:src/hooks/perps/usePerfdbSubscriptions.ts:35, :68) keep their names on the gateway endpoint."
