do_1 = "Book aggregates active limit orders per market and price level (bids from isLong true, asks from isLong false) from orders and OrderPlaced, OrderExecuted, OrderCancelled and OrderExpired deltas; snapshots carry up to 100 levels per side, asks ascending and bids descending (Hyperpax:data_api.md:214, Hyperpax:data_api.md:341)."
do_2 = "Live book frames are coalesced to at most 10 per second per topic and carry the top 20 levels per side; every 5 seconds a frame carries checksum, the CRC32 (IEEE) of the top 20 levels written as price:size pairs joined by commas, asks then bids (contracts/data-services.md:574)."
do_3 = "topics.go registers the providers <SYMBOL>@orderbook, @trade, @stats, @kline_<interval>, @perp_orderbook, @perp_trade, @perp_stats, @market, markets@all, markets@totals, chain@blocks and chain@transactions with the payloads of Hyperpax:data_api.md:234, Hyperpax:data_api.md:267, Hyperpax:data_api.md:287, Hyperpax:data_api.md:364, Hyperpax:data_api.md:388, Hyperpax:data_api.md:498, Hyperpax:data_api.md:513, Hyperpax:data_api.md:534, Hyperpax:data_api.md:611 and Hyperpax:data_api.md:647."
do_4 = "Kline snapshots honour limit with default 1000 and maximum 5000 (Hyperpax:data_api.md:292-293); on rollover the provider emits the previous candle with closed 1 and then the new candle with closed 0 (Hyperpax:data_api.md:337-339)."
do_5 = "Stats and market providers broadcast every 30 seconds and every 5 seconds respectively and on subscribe; @market broadcasts only while it has a subscriber (contracts/data-services.md:574)."
do_6 = "Add TestFeeds with one subtest per topic family plus book_ordering, book_rate_limit, book_checksum, kline_limit and kline_rollover (contracts/data-services.md:574)."

