do_1 = "Add store.WriteBlock(ctx, tx, block, rows) that inserts the perps.blocks row, every decoded fact row and every raw_logs row of the block and advances perps.cursors, in the order of CommitCanonical (Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/store/canonical.go:66) and under the single-writer lease of AcquireLease (Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/store/canonical.go:257)."
do_2 = "Inserts use ON CONFLICT (tx_hash, log_index) DO NOTHING, so a block written twice leaves one row per log and the second write changes nothing."
do_3 = "Every decoded row also lands in perps.protocol_events (event_name, args jsonb) and every venue transaction in perps.tx_actions with its explorer action; the watermark read of GetCanonicalWatermark (Launch-x:core/indexer/internal/store/canonical.go:453) becomes store.Cursor."
do_4 = "Each fact row is enqueued on the outbox in the same transaction through delivery.Store.Enqueue (Launch-x:shared/delivery/store.go:137), so a row exists in Postgres if and only if its message is pending or published."
do_5 = "Add TestFactWriters with subtests one_row_per_log, duplicate_block_noop, outbox_in_same_tx, cursor_advances and lease_refuses_second_writer against PERPS_DATA_TEST_DATABASE_URL."
