ac_23 = "The cross-feature rule of activation gating of the new addresses and stores at plan v6.12.0 is applied by resolution 9.63, 9.64, 9.65 and referenced by tasks 1.2.1, 1.2.2, 4.2.1, 5.2.3, 1.3.102, 3.2.12, 4.1.15, 5.1.13, 2.2.12, 2.2.13."
ac_24 = "The cross-feature rule of revert data per contract file, classified by the application is applied by resolution 9.66 and referenced by tasks 3.2.2, 4.2.8, 5.2.2, 6.2.9, 2.1.3, 2.2.9."
ac_25 = "The cross-feature rule of venue custody in the perps and spot module accounts is applied by resolution 9.67, 9.68 and referenced by tasks 3.0.4, 3.1.3, 3.1.19, 4.1.4, 4.3.2, 2.1.4, 2.2.16."
ac_26 = "The cross-feature rule of release work on the wired tree is applied by resolution 9.69 and referenced by tasks 1.3.100, 8.4.1, 8.4.2, 8.4.10."
ac_27 = "Resolution 9.1 holds: The plan table registers ActivationUpgrade, V610Upgrade, V6120Upgrade and MergeUpgrade: the V611Upgrade constant (node/upgrades.go:104-112), its handler registration (node/upgrades.go:204-206) and its entry in knownUpgradePlans (node/upgrades.go:532-534) are removed, and no store, tag line or test names v6.11 as a plan."
ac_28 = "Resolution 9.2 holds: runV6120Upgrade runs the module migrations, moveSidioraMintAuthority (node/upgrades_v611.go:115) and migrateSIDHolders (node/upgrades_v611.go:141) once, before the first domain hook, so the usid mint authority and the legacy SID balances of the SID proxy (node/upgrades_v611.go:24-26) move at the v6.12.0 height."
ac_29 = "Resolution 9.3 holds: GovernanceActivationUpgrade (modules/layerxcustody/types/governance_activation.go:5) names v6.12.0, so the custody proposal executes from the v6.12.0 done height that the folded v6.11 change set used to gate."
ac_30 = "Resolution 9.4 holds: tools/release/version.json (tools/release/version.json:2-3) carries version v6.12.0 and upgrade v6.12.0; the release build, the upgrade-info document and the tag read that identity and none of them names v6.11."
ac_31 = "Resolution 9.5 holds: The launchpad precompile at 0x1017 (modules/launchpad/types/keys.go:26) presents the function, event and error set of the deployment generation whose manifest status is active (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:7), with the same selectors, encodings and revert data."
ac_32 = "Resolution 9.6 holds: The launchpad hook MigrateV6120(ctx sdk.Context, k Keeper, evm EVMReader) error in modules/launchpad/keeper/migrate_v6120.go reads the pools of the first and the current deployment generation at the halt height and writes them into keeper state; the baseline handler calls it as the first of the four domain hooks and aborts the plan on its error."
ac_33 = "Resolution 9.7 holds: For every migrated pool, getReserves() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/interfaces/ISidioraPool.sol:65-69) through the precompile at the first post-upgrade height returns virtualUsdl, realUsdl and tokenReserve equal word for word to the contract read at the halt height; the rehearsal and the fleet check assert it."
ac_34 = "Resolution 9.8 holds: Pool creation, swaps, fee accrual and graduation move uusdl, the launchpad quote denom (modules/launchpad/types/params.go:31), at six decimals with BankKeeper.SendCoins (modules/launchpad/types/expected_keepers.go:16) between the bank accounts of the EVM addresses of the contract flow (modules/evm/keeper/address.go:58); each pool keeps its reserves in the bank account of the pool address, and the launchpad module account (ModuleAddress, modules/launchpad/keeper/keeper.go:40) only mints uusdl during the USDL migration step."
ac_35 = "Resolution 9.9 holds: The optical hooks of the launchpad contracts (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/BaseOptical.sol:12, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/OpticalRegistry.sol:14) are called by the launchpad precompile through evm.Call at the points of the contract flow; each migrated pool keeps its optical address and the optical contracts stay deployed and unchanged."
ac_36 = "Resolution 9.10 holds: Fee rights keep the ERC721 surface of SidioraNFT (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraNFT.sol:14) in both collections, keyed by collection and id, and pool tokens become tokenfactory denoms whose SidioraERC20 role is served at the old token address; transfer, approval and balance calls are served by the chain and their logs are visible to the explorer."
ac_37 = "Resolution 9.11 holds: Taker and maker fees of the perpetuals venue are the tier rates of the account's rolling 14-day volume as written in the parameter sheet; a taker fee rounds up to the uusdl unit and a negative maker rate is a rebate paid from perps_fees, rounded down."
ac_38 = "Resolution 9.12 holds: Every account has one USDL cross-margin balance over all markets; initial and maintenance margin come from the per-market notional tier tables, and setMarginMode accepts only the cross mode."
ac_39 = "Resolution 9.13 holds: No order or position exceeds 1000x leverage or the lower maximum of its market; the per-market maxima equal the maxLeverage values the Hyperpax application lists (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:168-185)."
ac_40 = "Resolution 9.14 holds: Premium samples are taken against the pricefeed index at least five seconds of block time apart, and funding settles once per hour of block time with the formula of the parameter sheet."
ac_41 = "Resolution 9.15 holds: The borrowing fee accrues hourly on open interest at the rate of the parameter sheet and is split between perps_fees and perps_insurance as that sheet states."
ac_42 = "Resolution 9.16 holds: An account whose equity is below its maintenance margin is liquidated against the book in slices, starting with partial closes, within the per-block bounds of the EndBlock pass."
ac_43 = "Resolution 9.17 holds: An account below two thirds of maintenance is taken over by the insurance fund perps_insurance; a deficit the fund cannot cover is closed by auto-deleveraging of ranked counterparties."
ac_44 = "Resolution 9.18 holds: SeedV6120(ctx sdk.Context, k Keeper) error in modules/perps/keeper/seed_v6120.go writes PAX, SID, NAS100, ETH, SPX500, BTC, BNB, SOL, HYPE, TSLA, GOOGL, XAU, NVDA, ASTER, LINK, XRP, TRUMP and AVAX with the market table and tier classes of contracts/perps-markets.md, and the fleet check reads all eighteen after the upgrade."
ac_45 = "Resolution 9.19 holds: The price-sidecar binary built from platform/hosted/feeder reads the Chainflow ticker of every listed market, accepts a ticker only when its symbol field equals the response symbol, and is installed per validator from tools/price-sidecar."
ac_46 = "Resolution 9.20 holds: The sidecar signs at most one MsgSubmitPrices per block with its feed key, encoded by the Cosmos transaction encoder of the feeder crate and decoded byte for byte by the Go side of the cross-language vector."
ac_47 = "Resolution 9.21 holds: Per enabled market in id order, the index is the two-pass median of fresh observations of the bonded set with required = max(min_sources, floor(bonded / 2) + 1), and the mark follows the smoothed-basis formula; below the required count the aggregate is not updated."
ac_48 = "Resolution 9.22 holds: GetPrice(ctx, marketId) returns a Fresh flag; the perpetuals and spot keepers refuse orders, fills and liquidations on a market while Fresh is false."
ac_49 = "Resolution 9.23 holds: A MsgSubmitPrices from a registered feed account of a bonded validator pays no fee and passes the size and rate decorators; any other submission is refused at the ante step."
ac_50 = "Resolution 9.24 holds: Every selector, event topic and error selector served by the spot precompile set equals the PECOR ABI the Hyperpax application encodes (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:5); the golden fixtures freeze it."
ac_51 = "Resolution 9.25 holds: Pools, vault shares, order records, active lists and fee accruals are keeper records of modules/spot; the feasibility record marks every PECOR method servable, so no method falls back to the continuous order book at this revision."
ac_52 = "Resolution 9.26 holds: Limit, stop-limit and stop-loss orders execute in the spot EndBlocker against the pricefeed index price; the execute and batch methods stay callable and apply the same rule inside a transaction."
ac_53 = "Resolution 9.27 holds: perps-gateway serves the symbol, markets, venue and spot user REST routes and the shared WebSocket with snapshot, dense sequence and resume from JetStream, in the data protocol the Hyperpax application already speaks."
ac_54 = "Resolution 9.28 holds: The GraphQL endpoint answers every query, mutation and subscription of the application's operation set unchanged, and the application pins that set against the gateway contract."
ac_55 = "Resolution 9.29 holds: perps-explorer serves per-account and per-market trading history from the fact tables and attaches to each row the transaction link built from PERPS_EXPLORER_TX_BASE."
ac_56 = "Resolution 9.30 holds: perps-portal renders the markets, account, leaderboard and venue statistics pages server-side from the gateway."
ac_57 = "Resolution 9.31 holds: The project perps-data declares perps-indexer, perps-gateway, perps-explorer, perps-portal, perps-replay, its own Postgres and a three-node NATS JetStream cluster; variables are named only, and only the gateway, explorer and portal have a public domain."
ac_58 = "Resolution 9.32 holds: The indexer, replay tool, gateway, explorer and portal are packages of the root module under platform/perps-data, and the decoders load the ABIs that precompiles/perps, precompiles/spot and precompiles/pricefeed export, so an ABI change and its decoder change land in one commit."
ac_59 = "Resolution 9.33 holds: From the v6.12.0 done height a call to 0x1015 (modules/layerxexchange/types/ids.go:15) executes precompiles/perps; the address keeps its activation entry (node/upgrades.go:496) and is switched by exchangeVersionSwitch in the shape of precompiles/p256/setup.go:15-24."
ac_60 = "Resolution 9.34 holds: precompiles/layerxexchange/legacy/v69 holds the v6.9 exchange (precompiles/layerxexchange/layerxexchange.go:140) unchanged apart from package clause and import paths, and recorded v6.9 calls replay on it with identical return data and logs."
ac_61 = "Resolution 9.35 holds: GetVersioned of precompiles/layerxexchange/setup.go:10-14 lists v6.9 beside the latest version, and GetCustomPrecompilesVersions (modules/evm/keeper/keeper.go:356-385) resolves a traced or replayed height below the done height to v6.9."
ac_62 = "Resolution 9.36 holds: Halt height, upgrade height, maintenance window, public notice text, build host and release id appear in docs/rollout-runbook.md as table rows without values; a release test refuses a public copy with any of them filled."
ac_63 = "Resolution 9.37 holds: Every rollout step takes its heights and hosts from the env file named on its command line (--env-file .env.rollout-v6120) and writes receipts with counts only under tools/release/rollout/v6.12.0."
ac_64 = "Resolution 9.38 holds: USDL is migrated to the bank denom uusdl (six decimals) whose ERC20 native pointer sits at the existing USDL address 0x85FcD13735F4309833A503EE804ea32395851479 (contracts/libraries/Constants.sol:14-16), so GetERC20NativePointer(ctx, \"uusdl\") (precompiles/utils/expected_keepers.go:127) returns that address before any venue hook runs."
ac_65 = "Resolution 9.39 holds: A token argument of 0x1015 must equal GetERC20NativePointer(ctx, \"uusdl\"); any other address reverts LXP_PERPS_UNSUPPORTED_COLLATERAL before a bank move, and collateral moves by bank SendCoins (precompiles/utils/expected_keepers.go:100) between the caller and the perps module account."
ac_66 = "Resolution 9.40 holds: The spot venue registers uusdl as its stable token at price 1e18 and checks the stable token argument against GetERC20NativePointer(ctx, \"uusdl\"); inbound amounts move by bank SendCoins to the spot module account with no allowance read."
ac_67 = "Resolution 9.41 holds: The perpetuals collateral entry (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:75-79) and the spot USDL entry name the one USDL address of contracts/libraries/Constants.sol:14 with six decimals, and every collateral amount is parsed at six decimals."
ac_68 = "Resolution 9.42 holds: The PAX token argument is the ERC20 native pointer of the base denom uhpx (modules/evm/keeper/params.go:22) and the SID token argument is the native pointer of usid; a token argument resolves to its denom through GetNativePointee (modules/evm/keeper/pointer.go:444) and decimals come from denom metadata."
ac_69 = "Resolution 9.43 holds: No wrapped PAX exists: native value attached to a spot call moves value / 1e12 uhpx, WETH() returns the uhpx pointer, and the application sells PAX from the native balance without a wrap step."
ac_70 = "Resolution 9.44 holds: Market id k of modules/pricefeed is the marketId k the Hyperpax application lists (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:168-185): 0 BTC, 1 ETH, 2 SOL, 3 AVAX, 4 LINK, 5 TSLA, 6 NVDA, 7 NAS100, 8 XAU, 9 SPX500, 10 GOOGL, 11 PAX, 12 SID, 13 HYPE, 14 XRP, 15 ASTER, 16 TRUMP, 17 BNB; ids are dense and never reused."
ac_71 = "Resolution 9.45 holds: Perpetual market k reads GetPrice(ctx, k) of the same symbol; the eighteen seeded markets carry the ids of the pricefeed table."
ac_72 = "Resolution 9.46 holds: The spot keeper prices uhpx from pricefeed market 11 and usid from market 12, and InitV6120 registers them with those ids."
ac_73 = "Resolution 9.47 holds: The indexer subjects, fact rows and gateway routes key a market by the pricefeed market id, so a perpetual fill, a mark update and an oracle aggregate of one symbol share one key."
ac_74 = "Resolution 9.48 holds: A call to 0x1015 at a height below the v6.12.0 done height executes layerxexchangev69 and at or above it executes precompiles/perps; perpsLive reads GetDoneHeight(ctx, V6120Upgrade) > 0 as xwebLive does (node/upgrades.go:255-262)."
ac_75 = "Resolution 9.49 holds: In every block from the activation height the price aggregate is written first, the perps EndBlocker runs second, the spot EndBlocker third and EvmKeeper.EndBlock last, all after oracle.EndBlocker (node/legacyabci/end_block.go:25-26); below the activation height none of the three venue steps runs."
ac_76 = "Resolution 9.50 holds: Logs emitted by the perps and spot EndBlock passes and the spot activation are written as one synthetic receipt per pass with SetTransientReceipt (modules/evm/keeper/receipt.go:28-36), each log converted by ConvertSyntheticEthLog (modules/evm/keeper/log.go:109-113)."
ac_77 = "Resolution 9.51 holds: runV6120Upgrade calls MigrateV6120, pricefeed InitV6120, SeedV6120 and spot InitV6120 in that order and refuses the plan when any hook is unbound."
ac_78 = "Resolution 9.52 holds: Each state change of the launchpad, perpetuals, spot and pricefeed precompiles, in a transaction or in EndBlock, emits the EVM log whose signature its contract file lists, from the precompile address that owns the state."
ac_79 = "Resolution 9.53 holds: The indexer decodes every log of 0x1015, 0x1020 and the spot set into the fact tables in one transaction per block, and positions, orders and accounts are reconstructed from those events with no state read."
ac_80 = "Resolution 9.54 holds: The fee in bps of one spot trade is the rail base (swapFeeBps at 0x1021, orderFeeBps at 0x1022 and 0x1023) plus tier1FeeBps from 10,000e18 USD of that trade and tier2FeeBps on top from 100,000e18, per trade with no rolling volume."
ac_81 = "Resolution 9.55 holds: Only the perps keeper writes and reads the perpetuals volume buckets keyed by floor(blockTime / 86400); the spot keeper keeps no volume buckets and reads none."
ac_82 = "Resolution 9.56 holds: PECOR 0x1021, PECOROrders 0x1022, PECORStopOrders 0x1023, PECORQuoter 0x1024 and PECORVault 0x1025 are served from the v6.12.0 done height, and the application address module defaults to exactly these five addresses."
ac_83 = "Resolution 9.57 holds: 0x1026 (PECORVaultShare) and 0x1027 (PECORRouter) carry no code before or after activation; vault share Transfer and Approval logs come from the share pointer addresses returned by shareTokens(address), and the indexer decodes them by those addresses rather than by 0x1026."
ac_84 = "Resolution 9.58 holds: A bonded validator operator registers one 33-byte compressed secp256k1 key through registerFeedKey(bytes) at 0x1020; a key replaces the previous one, a feed account belongs to one validator, and only keys of bonded validators count."
ac_85 = "Resolution 9.59 holds: InitV6120 registers no feed key; each operator registers a key and starts the sidecar after activation, and the rollout oracle phase checks one registered key per validator and a fresh price on every market."
ac_86 = "Resolution 9.60 holds: Deployment and install files of this release carry variable names and empty host fields only: the runbook input rows, the data-services Railway layout and the sidecar config template name inputs without values."
ac_87 = "Resolution 9.61 holds: The .sol files of precompiles/perps and precompiles/pricefeed are interface declarations that generate abi.json; the release deploys no venue contract, and the application drops the Diamond address (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:10-11) and the per-user vault hook."
ac_88 = "Resolution 9.62 holds: The spot contract table of the application (Hyperpax:src/core/spot/addresses.ts:31-59) points PECOR, Quoter, Orders, StopOrders and Vault at the precompile set, maps the price oracle to 0x1020 and removes the transaction tracker."
ac_89 = "Resolution 9.63 holds: 0x1020 to 0x1027 sit under one v6.12.0 activation entry and answer as accounts without code below the done height; the giga executor fails fast on them as it does on late custom precompiles (engine/executor/precompiles/failfast.go:116-117)."
ac_90 = "Resolution 9.64 holds: The v6.12.0 store upgrades add the perps, spot and pricefeed store keys beside activationStoreUpgrades (node/upgrades.go:398-402), and each module registers with consensus version 1."
ac_91 = "Resolution 9.65 holds: 0x1017 stays behind activationPrecompileGate (node/upgrades.go:498), and GetVersioned of precompiles/launchpad returns the new precompile for the latest upgrade and the current one under v6.10 from precompiles/launchpad/legacy/v610, in the shape of precompiles/p256/setup.go:15-24."
ac_92 = "Resolution 9.66 holds: Perpetuals and pricefeed reverts carry Error(string) whose text starts with the LXP code (precompiles/common/precompiles.go:134-143); spot and launchpad reverts carry ABI custom error data; the application decodes both before its generic classification."
ac_93 = "Resolution 9.67 holds: The perps module account holds every uusdl of the perpetuals venue, including the balances of perps_fees and perps_insurance; the spot module account holds every spot denom, with book reserves, escrows and fee accruals kept as keeper records over that one balance."
ac_94 = "Resolution 9.68 holds: The launchpad module account (modules/launchpad/keeper/keeper.go:40, modules/launchpad/types/keys.go:10) gains Minter permission for step 1 of MigrateV6120 and keeps no escrow for pool reserves; launchpad_treasury (modules/launchpad/types/keys.go:14) stays as it is."
ac_95 = "Resolution 9.69 holds: The baseline wiring task requires every domain completion task, and the release tasks require the wiring task, so the release candidate is built from a tree where every domain package set passed once."
ac_96 = "Every applies_to id of every [resolution.9.k] names a task or capability that exists in the assembled spec/release-v6-12-0/spec.kvx; tools/spec/check_resolutions.py prints each unresolved id as resolution.<id>: unknown <ref> and exits 1."
ac_97 = "Every [decision.N] of the head (decision.1 to decision.11) is named by the source \"decision DN\" of at least one resolution, and every resolution applies to at least one task id (a capability alone does not satisfy it)."
ac_98 = "contracts/address-table.md lists every precompile address of the resolutions (0x1015, 0x1017, 0x1020 to 0x1027) with its constructor and activation rule, and contracts/README.md lists every contract file under parts/contracts with its reading order."

[contract_context.9.address_table]
launchpad = "0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001017 is the launchpad precompile (modules/launchpad/types/keys.go:26), built by precompiles/launchpad NewPrecompile (precompiles/launchpad/launchpad.go:180), registered in the versioned set (precompiles/setup.go:183) and activated with module launchpad under ActivationUpgrade v6.9 (node/upgrades.go:93, node/upgrades.go:498)."
perps = "0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001015 (modules/layerxexchange/types/ids.go:15) keeps its activation entry with module layerxexchange (node/upgrades.go:496); from the v6.12.0 done height it is served by precompiles/perps NewPrecompile and below it by layerxexchangev69.NewPrecompile, the copy of precompiles/layerxexchange/layerxexchange.go:140."
pricefeed = "0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001020 is served by precompiles/pricefeed NewPrecompile with module pricefeed under the v6.12.0 activation entry."
spot = "0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001021 to 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000001025 are served by the entries of precompiles/spot NewPrecompileSet with module spot under the v6.12.0 activation entry; 0x1026 and 0x1027 sit under the same entry and carry no code."
activation = "Every new address is gated in the shape of activationPrecompileGate (node/upgrades.go:489-503) through SetCustomPrecompileActivation (modules/evm/keeper/keeper.go:207-241); the versioned set is resolved per height by GetCustomPrecompilesVersions (modules/evm/keeper/keeper.go:356-385)."
module_accounts = "The launchpad module account is authtypes.NewModuleAddress(ModuleName) (modules/launchpad/keeper/keeper.go:40, modules/launchpad/types/keys.go:10) with Minter permission for the USDL step, beside launchpad_treasury (modules/launchpad/types/keys.go:14); pool reserves stay in the bank accounts of the pool addresses; the perps module adds perps, perps_fees and perps_insurance and the spot module adds spot."
tokens = "uusdl is the launchpad quote denom (modules/launchpad/types/params.go:31) whose pointer sits at the USDL address of contracts/libraries/Constants.sol:14; uhpx is the base denom (modules/evm/keeper/params.go:22); usid receives the legacy SID balances of the SID proxy (node/upgrades_v611.go:24-26); every pointer is read with GetERC20NativePointer (precompiles/utils/expected_keepers.go:127) and resolved back with GetNativePointee (modules/evm/keeper/pointer.go:444)."

[contract_context.9.conformance]
clause_check = "The repository spec linter already refuses a resolution whose applies_to names an unknown clause (tools/specgen/validate.go:117-125, clauseExists at tools/specgen/validate.go:132); the release check resolves applies_to against task and capability ids, which that clause lookup does not."
parser = "The check reads the kvx with the section, key and list rules of tools/specgen/kvx.go (ParseFile at tools/specgen/kvx.go:36, List at tools/specgen/kvx.go:137, SectionsWithPrefix at tools/specgen/kvx.go:204)."
shape = "A resolution carries title, contract, applies_to and source, the shape of the resolutions of spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx."
source = "A source is either decision DN, naming [decision.N] of the head, or contract <file>#<heading>, naming a heading of a file under contracts/ or docs/ of the feature."

[resolution.9.1]
title = "Plan v6.11 leaves the plan table"
contract = "The plan table registers ActivationUpgrade, V610Upgrade, V6120Upgrade and MergeUpgrade: the V611Upgrade constant (node/upgrades.go:104-112), its handler registration (node/upgrades.go:204-206) and its entry in knownUpgradePlans (node/upgrades.go:532-534) are removed, and no store, tag line or test names v6.11 as a plan."
applies_to = ["1.0.3", "1.0.4", "1.2.1"]
source = "decision D1"

[resolution.9.2]
title = "The v6.12.0 handler carries every change of v6.11"
contract = "runV6120Upgrade runs the module migrations, moveSidioraMintAuthority (node/upgrades_v611.go:115) and migrateSIDHolders (node/upgrades_v611.go:141) once, before the first domain hook, so the usid mint authority and the legacy SID balances of the SID proxy (node/upgrades_v611.go:24-26) move at the v6.12.0 height."
applies_to = ["1.0.3", "1.0.4", "1.2.3"]
source = "decision D1"

[resolution.9.3]
title = "The custody governance gate moves to v6.12.0"
contract = "GovernanceActivationUpgrade (modules/layerxcustody/types/governance_activation.go:5) names v6.12.0, so the custody proposal executes from the v6.12.0 done height that the folded v6.11 change set used to gate."
applies_to = ["1.0.5"]
source = "decision D1"

[resolution.9.4]
title = "Release identity is v6.12.0"
contract = "tools/release/version.json (tools/release/version.json:2-3) carries version v6.12.0 and upgrade v6.12.0; the release build, the upgrade-info document and the tag read that identity and none of them names v6.11."
applies_to = ["8.4.1", "8.4.5", "8.4.14", "1.0.1"]
source = "decision D1"

[resolution.9.5]
title = "The launchpad precompile serves the manifest-active generation"
contract = "The launchpad precompile at 0x1017 (modules/launchpad/types/keys.go:26) presents the function, event and error set of the deployment generation whose manifest status is active (Launch-x:shared/config/deployment/current.json:7), with the same selectors, encodings and revert data."
applies_to = ["2.0.1", "2.0.2", "2.0.3", "2.0.4", "2.0.5", "2.2.1", "2.2.2", "2.2.3", "2.2.4", "2.2.5", "2.2.6", "2.2.7", "2.3.6", "2.3.9"]
source = "decision D2"

[resolution.9.6]
title = "Both deployment generations migrate into the precompile"
contract = "The launchpad hook MigrateV6120(ctx sdk.Context, k Keeper, evm EVMReader) error in modules/launchpad/keeper/migrate_v6120.go reads the pools of the first and the current deployment generation at the halt height and writes them into keeper state; the baseline handler calls it as the first of the four domain hooks and aborts the plan on its error."
applies_to = ["2.2.14", "2.2.15", "2.2.16", "2.2.17", "2.2.18", "1.0.3", "1.3.100"]
source = "decision D2"

[resolution.9.7]
title = "Migrated pools read the same through 0x1017"
contract = "For every migrated pool, getReserves() (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/interfaces/ISidioraPool.sol:65-69) through the precompile at the first post-upgrade height returns virtualUsdl, realUsdl and tokenReserve equal word for word to the contract read at the halt height; the rehearsal and the fleet check assert it."
applies_to = ["8.4.10", "8.4.12", "8.4.13", "8.5.11", "2.2.15", "2.2.18"]
source = "decision D2"

[resolution.9.8]
title = "Launchpad quotes in USDL through its module account"
contract = "Pool creation, swaps, fee accrual and graduation move uusdl, the launchpad quote denom (modules/launchpad/types/params.go:31), at six decimals with BankKeeper.SendCoins (modules/launchpad/types/expected_keepers.go:16) between the bank accounts of the EVM addresses of the contract flow (modules/evm/keeper/address.go:58); each pool keeps its reserves in the bank account of the pool address, and the launchpad module account (ModuleAddress, modules/launchpad/keeper/keeper.go:40) only mints uusdl during the USDL migration step."
applies_to = ["2.1.2", "2.1.5", "2.1.6", "2.1.7", "2.2.3", "2.2.16"]
source = "decision D3"

[resolution.9.9]
title = "The hook system ships with the release"
contract = "The optical hooks of the launchpad contracts (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/BaseOptical.sol:12, Launch-x:contracts/contracts/opticals/OpticalRegistry.sol:14) are called by the launchpad precompile through evm.Call at the points of the contract flow; each migrated pool keeps its optical address and the optical contracts stay deployed and unchanged."
applies_to = ["2.1.1", "2.2.10", "2.2.17"]
source = "decision D3"

[resolution.9.10]
title = "Fee rights are ERC721 and pool tokens are ERC20"
contract = "Fee rights keep the ERC721 surface of SidioraNFT (Launch-x:contracts/contracts/core/SidioraNFT.sol:14) in both collections, keyed by collection and id, and pool tokens become tokenfactory denoms whose SidioraERC20 role is served at the old token address; transfer, approval and balance calls are served by the chain and their logs are visible to the explorer."
applies_to = ["2.1.9", "2.2.7", "2.2.17"]
source = "decision D3"

[resolution.9.11]
title = "Trading fees follow the volume tier table"
contract = "Taker and maker fees of the perpetuals venue are the tier rates of the account's rolling 14-day volume as written in the parameter sheet; a taker fee rounds up to the uusdl unit and a negative maker rate is a rebate paid from perps_fees, rounded down."
applies_to = ["3.0.4", "3.1.10", "3.2.6"]
source = "contract contracts/perps-parameters.md#1-trading-fees"

[resolution.9.12]
title = "Margin is cross with tiered maintenance"
contract = "Every account has one USDL cross-margin balance over all markets; initial and maintenance margin come from the per-market notional tier tables, and setMarginMode accepts only the cross mode."
applies_to = ["3.0.5", "3.1.4", "3.2.3"]
source = "contract contracts/perps-parameters.md#2-margin"

[resolution.9.13]
title = "Leverage is capped at 1000x"
contract = "No order or position exceeds 1000x leverage or the lower maximum of its market; the per-market maxima equal the maxLeverage values the Hyperpax application lists (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:168-185)."
applies_to = ["3.0.5", "3.1.7", "3.2.11"]
source = "contract contracts/perps-parameters.md#9-consequences-of-the-1000x-cap"

[resolution.9.14]
title = "Funding settles every hour from the premium"
contract = "Premium samples are taken against the pricefeed index at least five seconds of block time apart, and funding settles once per hour of block time with the formula of the parameter sheet."
applies_to = ["3.1.12", "3.2.9"]
source = "contract contracts/perps-parameters.md#3-funding"

[resolution.9.15]
title = "Borrowing fee accrues on open interest"
contract = "The borrowing fee accrues hourly on open interest at the rate of the parameter sheet and is split between perps_fees and perps_insurance as that sheet states."
applies_to = ["3.1.13", "3.2.9"]
source = "contract contracts/perps-parameters.md#4-borrowing-fee-on-open-interest"

[resolution.9.16]
title = "Liquidation is account-level with partial close"
contract = "An account whose equity is below its maintenance margin is liquidated against the book in slices, starting with partial closes, within the per-block bounds of the EndBlock pass."
applies_to = ["3.1.14", "3.2.5", "3.2.9"]
source = "contract contracts/perps-parameters.md#6-liquidation"

[resolution.9.17]
title = "Backstop, insurance and auto-deleveraging"
contract = "An account below two thirds of maintenance is taken over by the insurance fund perps_insurance; a deficit the fund cannot cover is closed by auto-deleveraging of ranked counterparties."
applies_to = ["3.1.15", "3.1.16"]
source = "contract contracts/perps-parameters.md#7-insurance-fund-and-auto-deleveraging"

[resolution.9.18]
title = "Eighteen markets open at activation"
contract = "SeedV6120(ctx sdk.Context, k Keeper) error in modules/perps/keeper/seed_v6120.go writes PAX, SID, NAS100, ETH, SPX500, BTC, BNB, SOL, HYPE, TSLA, GOOGL, XAU, NVDA, ASTER, LINK, XRP, TRUMP and AVAX with the market table and tier classes of contracts/perps-markets.md, and the fleet check reads all eighteen after the upgrade."
applies_to = ["3.0.5", "3.2.11", "8.4.10"]
source = "decision D4"

[resolution.9.19]
title = "Each validator runs a sidecar on the Chainflow feed"
contract = "The price-sidecar binary built from platform/hosted/feeder reads the Chainflow ticker of every listed market, accepts a ticker only when its symbol field equals the response symbol, and is installed per validator from tools/price-sidecar."
applies_to = ["5.2.4", "5.2.5", "5.2.6", "5.2.7"]
source = "decision D5"

[resolution.9.20]
title = "One signed submission per validator per block"
contract = "The sidecar signs at most one MsgSubmitPrices per block with its feed key, encoded by the Cosmos transaction encoder of the feeder crate and decoded byte for byte by the Go side of the cross-language vector."
applies_to = ["5.0.3", "5.1.3", "5.1.10", "5.1.14", "5.1.15", "5.3.2"]
source = "decision D5"

[resolution.9.21]
title = "The chain aggregates per block over the bonded set"
contract = "Per enabled market in id order, the index is the two-pass median of fresh observations of the bonded set with required = max(min_sources, floor(bonded / 2) + 1), and the mark follows the smoothed-basis formula; below the required count the aggregate is not updated."
applies_to = ["5.1.7", "5.1.8", "5.3.1"]
source = "decision D5"

[resolution.9.22]
title = "Venues refuse trading on a stale price"
contract = "GetPrice(ctx, marketId) returns a Fresh flag; the perpetuals and spot keepers refuse orders, fills and liquidations on a market while Fresh is false."
applies_to = ["5.1.9", "3.1.11", "4.1.5"]
source = "decision D5"

[resolution.9.23]
title = "Price submissions pay no fee and are bounded"
contract = "A MsgSubmitPrices from a registered feed account of a bonded validator pays no fee and passes the size and rate decorators; any other submission is refused at the ante step."
applies_to = ["5.1.12"]
source = "decision D5"

[resolution.9.24]
title = "The spot ABI equals the application ABI"
contract = "Every selector, event topic and error selector served by the spot precompile set equals the PECOR ABI the Hyperpax application encodes (Hyperpax:src/core/network/spot_abi/PECOR.ts:5); the golden fixtures freeze it."
applies_to = ["4.0.1", "4.0.2", "4.0.3", "4.0.4", "4.0.5", "4.0.6", "6.0.3"]
source = "decision D6"

[resolution.9.25]
title = "PECOR state lives in the spot keeper"
contract = "Pools, vault shares, order records, active lists and fee accruals are keeper records of modules/spot; the feasibility record marks every PECOR method servable, so no method falls back to the continuous order book at this revision."
applies_to = ["4.2.1", "4.2.2", "4.2.3", "4.2.4", "4.2.5", "4.2.6"]
source = "decision D6"

[resolution.9.26]
title = "Resting spot orders execute in EndBlock"
contract = "Limit, stop-limit and stop-loss orders execute in the spot EndBlocker against the pricefeed index price; the execute and batch methods stay callable and apply the same rule inside a transaction."
applies_to = ["4.1.8", "4.1.9", "4.2.9"]
source = "contract contracts/spot.md#endblock-execution"

[resolution.9.27]
title = "The gateway serves REST and the shared WebSocket"
contract = "perps-gateway serves the symbol, markets, venue and spot user REST routes and the shared WebSocket with snapshot, dense sequence and resume from JetStream, in the data protocol the Hyperpax application already speaks."
applies_to = ["7.2.1", "7.2.2", "7.2.3", "7.2.4", "7.2.5", "7.2.13", "7.2.14", "7.2.15", "7.2.16"]
source = "decision D7"

[resolution.9.28]
title = "GraphQL serves the full operation set"
contract = "The GraphQL endpoint answers every query, mutation and subscription of the application's operation set unchanged, and the application pins that set against the gateway contract."
applies_to = ["7.2.6", "7.2.7", "7.2.8", "7.2.9", "7.2.10", "7.2.19", "6.3.7"]
source = "decision D7"

[resolution.9.29]
title = "The chain explorer service links each row to the network explorer"
contract = "perps-explorer serves per-account and per-market trading history from the fact tables and attaches to each row the transaction link built from PERPS_EXPLORER_TX_BASE."
applies_to = ["7.2.11", "7.2.12"]
source = "decision D7"

[resolution.9.30]
title = "The portal renders markets, accounts and venue statistics"
contract = "perps-portal renders the markets, account, leaderboard and venue statistics pages server-side from the gateway."
applies_to = ["7.3.1", "7.3.2"]
source = "decision D7"

[resolution.9.31]
title = "A dedicated Railway project hosts the data services"
contract = "The project perps-data declares perps-indexer, perps-gateway, perps-explorer, perps-portal, perps-replay, its own Postgres and a three-node NATS JetStream cluster; variables are named only, and only the gateway, explorer and portal have a public domain."
applies_to = ["7.3.3", "7.3.4", "7.0.6"]
source = "decision D8"

[resolution.9.32]
title = "The data services live under platform/perps-data"
contract = "The indexer, replay tool, gateway, explorer and portal are packages of the root module under platform/perps-data, and the decoders load the ABIs that precompiles/perps, precompiles/spot and precompiles/pricefeed export, so an ABI change and its decoder change land in one commit."
applies_to = ["7.0.1", "7.0.2", "7.1.2", "7.1.3", "7.3.99"]
source = "decision D9"

[resolution.9.33]
title = "The perpetuals precompile serves 0x1015 from the done height"
contract = "From the v6.12.0 done height a call to 0x1015 (modules/layerxexchange/types/ids.go:15) executes precompiles/perps; the address keeps its activation entry (node/upgrades.go:496) and is switched by exchangeVersionSwitch in the shape of precompiles/p256/setup.go:15-24."
applies_to = ["1.2.1", "1.3.100", "3.2.1"]
source = "decision D10"

[resolution.9.34]
title = "The v6.9 exchange stays byte-identical under legacy/v69"
contract = "precompiles/layerxexchange/legacy/v69 holds the v6.9 exchange (precompiles/layerxexchange/layerxexchange.go:140) unchanged apart from package clause and import paths, and recorded v6.9 calls replay on it with identical return data and logs."
applies_to = ["3.0.8", "3.3.4"]
source = "decision D10"

[resolution.9.35]
title = "Historical heights select the version by height"
contract = "GetVersioned of precompiles/layerxexchange/setup.go:10-14 lists v6.9 beside the latest version, and GetCustomPrecompilesVersions (modules/evm/keeper/keeper.go:356-385) resolves a traced or replayed height below the done height to v6.9."
applies_to = ["3.2.13", "1.2.1"]
source = "decision D10"

[resolution.9.36]
title = "Operator inputs are blank fields in the public runbook"
contract = "Halt height, upgrade height, maintenance window, public notice text, build host and release id appear in docs/rollout-runbook.md as table rows without values; a release test refuses a public copy with any of them filled."
applies_to = ["8.5.1", "8.4.15"]
source = "decision D11"

[resolution.9.37]
title = "Rollout commands read inputs from an untracked env file"
contract = "Every rollout step takes its heights and hosts from the env file named on its command line (--env-file .env.rollout-v6120) and writes receipts with counts only under tools/release/rollout/v6.12.0."
applies_to = ["8.5.2", "8.5.3", "8.5.4", "8.5.5", "8.5.6", "8.5.7"]
source = "decision D11"

[resolution.9.38]
title = "USDL is the bank denom uusdl at its existing address"
contract = "USDL is migrated to the bank denom uusdl (six decimals) whose ERC20 native pointer sits at the existing USDL address 0x85FcD13735F4309833A503EE804ea32395851479 (contracts/libraries/Constants.sol:14-16), so GetERC20NativePointer(ctx, \"uusdl\") (precompiles/utils/expected_keepers.go:127) returns that address before any venue hook runs."
applies_to = ["2.2.14", "2.2.16", "1.0.3", "4.1.14"]
source = "contract contracts/spot.md#token-model"

[resolution.9.39]
title = "Perpetuals collateral is only the USDL pointer"
contract = "A token argument of 0x1015 must equal GetERC20NativePointer(ctx, \"uusdl\"); any other address reverts LXP_PERPS_UNSUPPORTED_COLLATERAL before a bank move, and collateral moves by bank SendCoins (precompiles/utils/expected_keepers.go:100) between the caller and the perps module account."
applies_to = ["3.0.7", "3.1.3", "3.2.3"]
source = "contract contracts/perps.md#2-units-and-encodings"

[resolution.9.40]
title = "The spot stable token is the USDL pointer"
contract = "The spot venue registers uusdl as its stable token at price 1e18 and checks the stable token argument against GetERC20NativePointer(ctx, \"uusdl\"); inbound amounts move by bank SendCoins to the spot module account with no allowance read."
applies_to = ["4.1.4", "4.1.14"]
source = "contract contracts/spot.md#token-model"

[resolution.9.41]
title = "The application uses one six-decimal USDL"
contract = "The perpetuals collateral entry (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:75-79) and the spot USDL entry name the one USDL address of contracts/libraries/Constants.sol:14 with six decimals, and every collateral amount is parsed at six decimals."
applies_to = ["6.2.4", "6.2.5", "6.2.6", "6.2.10"]
source = "contract contracts/application.md#amounts"

[resolution.9.42]
title = "PAX is uhpx and SID is usid through native pointers"
contract = "The PAX token argument is the ERC20 native pointer of the base denom uhpx (modules/evm/keeper/params.go:22) and the SID token argument is the native pointer of usid; a token argument resolves to its denom through GetNativePointee (modules/evm/keeper/pointer.go:444) and decimals come from denom metadata."
applies_to = ["4.1.4", "4.1.7", "4.1.14", "4.2.6"]
source = "contract contracts/spot.md#token-model"

[resolution.9.43]
title = "Native PAX and the PAX token are one balance"
contract = "No wrapped PAX exists: native value attached to a spot call moves value / 1e12 uhpx, WETH() returns the uhpx pointer, and the application sells PAX from the native balance without a wrap step."
applies_to = ["4.1.7", "4.2.2", "6.2.10", "6.2.11"]
source = "contract contracts/spot.md#token-model"

[resolution.9.44]
title = "Pricefeed market ids 0-17 follow the application's order"
contract = "Market id k of modules/pricefeed is the marketId k the Hyperpax application lists (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:168-185): 0 BTC, 1 ETH, 2 SOL, 3 AVAX, 4 LINK, 5 TSLA, 6 NVDA, 7 NAS100, 8 XAU, 9 SPX500, 10 GOOGL, 11 PAX, 12 SID, 13 HYPE, 14 XRP, 15 ASTER, 16 TRUMP, 17 BNB; ids are dense and never reused."
applies_to = ["5.0.2", "5.1.11", "5.2.3"]
source = "contract contracts/pricefeed.md#markets-and-chainflow-symbols"

[resolution.9.45]
title = "Perpetual market ids equal pricefeed market ids"
contract = "Perpetual market k reads GetPrice(ctx, k) of the same symbol; the eighteen seeded markets carry the ids of the pricefeed table."
applies_to = ["3.0.5", "3.1.11", "3.2.11"]
source = "contract contracts/perps-markets.md#2-market-table"

[resolution.9.46]
title = "Spot prices PAX from market 11 and SID from market 12"
contract = "The spot keeper prices uhpx from pricefeed market 11 and usid from market 12, and InitV6120 registers them with those ids."
applies_to = ["4.1.5", "4.1.14"]
source = "contract contracts/spot.md#token-model"

[resolution.9.47]
title = "Data services key market rows by the same id"
contract = "The indexer subjects, fact rows and gateway routes key a market by the pricefeed market id, so a perpetual fill, a mark update and an oracle aggregate of one symbol share one key."
applies_to = ["7.0.3", "7.1.2", "7.1.3"]
source = "contract contracts/data-services.md#3-nats-jetstream-stream-and-subjects"

[resolution.9.48]
title = "0x1015 switches version at the done height"
contract = "A call to 0x1015 at a height below the v6.12.0 done height executes layerxexchangev69 and at or above it executes precompiles/perps; perpsLive reads GetDoneHeight(ctx, V6120Upgrade) > 0 as xwebLive does (node/upgrades.go:255-262)."
applies_to = ["1.2.1", "1.3.100", "3.0.8", "3.2.13", "3.3.4"]
source = "contract contracts/perps.md#22-activation-and-versioning"

[resolution.9.49]
title = "End-block order is pricefeed, perps, spot, EVM"
contract = "In every block from the activation height the price aggregate is written first, the perps EndBlocker runs second, the spot EndBlocker third and EvmKeeper.EndBlock last, all after oracle.EndBlocker (node/legacyabci/end_block.go:25-26); below the activation height none of the three venue steps runs."
applies_to = ["1.3.103", "3.2.9", "4.2.9", "5.1.8", "5.1.13"]
source = "contract contracts/perps.md#23-endblock"

[resolution.9.50]
title = "EndBlock logs land in a synthetic receipt"
contract = "Logs emitted by the perps and spot EndBlock passes and the spot activation are written as one synthetic receipt per pass with SetTransientReceipt (modules/evm/keeper/receipt.go:28-36), each log converted by ConvertSyntheticEthLog (modules/evm/keeper/log.go:109-113)."
applies_to = ["3.2.10", "4.2.9", "4.1.14"]
source = "contract contracts/perps.md#23-endblock"

[resolution.9.51]
title = "Upgrade hooks run launchpad, pricefeed, perps, spot"
contract = "runV6120Upgrade calls MigrateV6120, pricefeed InitV6120, SeedV6120 and spot InitV6120 in that order and refuses the plan when any hook is unbound."
applies_to = ["1.0.3", "1.3.100", "2.2.17", "2.2.18", "3.2.11", "4.1.14", "5.1.11"]
source = "contract contracts/spot.md#activation"

[resolution.9.52]
title = "Every venue state change emits an EVM log"
contract = "Each state change of the launchpad, perpetuals, spot and pricefeed precompiles, in a transaction or in EndBlock, emits the EVM log whose signature its contract file lists, from the precompile address that owns the state."
applies_to = ["3.2.8", "4.2.7", "5.2.1", "2.2.8", "2.3.1", "2.3.3"]
source = "contract contracts/perps.md#18-events"

[resolution.9.53]
title = "The indexer rebuilds venue state from logs alone"
contract = "The indexer decodes every log of 0x1015, 0x1020 and the spot set into the fact tables in one transaction per block, and positions, orders and accounts are reconstructed from those events with no state read."
applies_to = ["7.1.2", "7.1.3", "7.1.4", "7.1.8", "3.3.3"]
source = "contract contracts/data-services.md#6-event-decoding"

[resolution.9.54]
title = "Spot fees follow the PECOR per-trade tier model"
contract = "The fee in bps of one spot trade is the rail base (swapFeeBps at 0x1021, orderFeeBps at 0x1022 and 0x1023) plus tier1FeeBps from 10,000e18 USD of that trade and tier2FeeBps on top from 100,000e18, per trade with no rolling volume."
applies_to = ["4.1.6", "4.1.13"]
source = "contract contracts/spot.md#fees"

[resolution.9.55]
title = "The 14-day volume buckets belong to the perps keeper alone"
contract = "Only the perps keeper writes and reads the perpetuals volume buckets keyed by floor(blockTime / 86400); the spot keeper keeps no volume buckets and reads none."
applies_to = ["3.1.10", "4.1.6"]
source = "contract contracts/perps-parameters.md#1-trading-fees"

[resolution.9.56]
title = "The spot set serves 0x1021-0x1025"
contract = "PECOR 0x1021, PECOROrders 0x1022, PECORStopOrders 0x1023, PECORQuoter 0x1024 and PECORVault 0x1025 are served from the v6.12.0 done height, and the application address module defaults to exactly these five addresses."
applies_to = ["1.2.1", "4.2.1", "6.0.1", "6.2.10"]
source = "contract contracts/spot.md#address-set"

[resolution.9.57]
title = "0x1026 and 0x1027 are not served"
contract = "0x1026 (PECORVaultShare) and 0x1027 (PECORRouter) carry no code before or after activation; vault share Transfer and Approval logs come from the share pointer addresses returned by shareTokens(address), and the indexer decodes them by those addresses rather than by 0x1026."
applies_to = ["4.1.11", "4.2.7", "7.1.3", "1.2.2"]
source = "contract contracts/spot.md#address-set"

[resolution.9.58]
title = "Feed keys are registered per validator with registerFeedKey"
contract = "A bonded validator operator registers one 33-byte compressed secp256k1 key through registerFeedKey(bytes) at 0x1020; a key replaces the previous one, a feed account belongs to one validator, and only keys of bonded validators count."
applies_to = ["5.1.5", "5.2.1", "5.2.2"]
source = "contract contracts/pricefeed.md#feed-key-registry"

[resolution.9.59]
title = "Rollout registers a key per validator before prices count"
contract = "InitV6120 registers no feed key; each operator registers a key and starts the sidecar after activation, and the rollout oracle phase checks one registered key per validator and a fresh price on every market."
applies_to = ["5.1.11", "5.3.1", "8.5.7"]
source = "contract contracts/pricefeed.md#activation"

[resolution.9.60]
title = "Operator inputs stay blank in every public file"
contract = "Deployment and install files of this release carry variable names and empty host fields only: the runbook input rows, the data-services Railway layout and the sidecar config template name inputs without values."
applies_to = ["8.5.1", "7.3.3", "5.2.7"]
source = "contract contracts/release.md#rollout"

[resolution.9.61]
title = "No Solidity venue contract is deployed"
contract = "The .sol files of precompiles/perps and precompiles/pricefeed are interface declarations that generate abi.json; the release deploys no venue contract, and the application drops the Diamond address (Hyperpax:src/core/perps/config.ts:10-11) and the per-user vault hook."
applies_to = ["3.0.1", "5.0.1", "6.3.1", "6.3.3"]
source = "contract contracts/perps.md#25-divergences-from-the-hyperpax-diamond-interface"

[resolution.9.62]
title = "Spot contract addresses move to the precompiles"
contract = "The spot contract table of the application (Hyperpax:src/core/spot/addresses.ts:31-59) points PECOR, Quoter, Orders, StopOrders and Vault at the precompile set, maps the price oracle to 0x1020 and removes the transaction tracker."
applies_to = ["6.2.10", "6.2.12"]
source = "contract contracts/application.md#address-table"

[resolution.9.63]
title = "New addresses have no code before the done height"
contract = "0x1020 to 0x1027 sit under one v6.12.0 activation entry and answer as accounts without code below the done height; the giga executor fails fast on them as it does on late custom precompiles (engine/executor/precompiles/failfast.go:116-117)."
applies_to = ["1.2.1", "1.2.2", "4.2.1", "5.2.3"]
source = "contract contracts/pricefeed.md#activation"

[resolution.9.64]
title = "Plan v6.12.0 adds the perps, spot and pricefeed stores"
contract = "The v6.12.0 store upgrades add the perps, spot and pricefeed store keys beside activationStoreUpgrades (node/upgrades.go:398-402), and each module registers with consensus version 1."
applies_to = ["1.3.102", "3.2.12", "4.1.15", "5.1.13"]
source = "contract contracts/release.md#build-and-plan"

[resolution.9.65]
title = "0x1017 keeps its gate and the current launchpad becomes legacy v6.10"
contract = "0x1017 stays behind activationPrecompileGate (node/upgrades.go:498), and GetVersioned of precompiles/launchpad returns the new precompile for the latest upgrade and the current one under v6.10 from precompiles/launchpad/legacy/v610, in the shape of precompiles/p256/setup.go:15-24."
applies_to = ["2.2.12", "2.2.13"]
source = "contract contracts/launchpad.md#16-activation"

[resolution.9.66]
title = "Revert data follows each contract file and the application classifies it"
contract = "Perpetuals and pricefeed reverts carry Error(string) whose text starts with the LXP code (precompiles/common/precompiles.go:134-143); spot and launchpad reverts carry ABI custom error data; the application decodes both before its generic classification."
applies_to = ["3.2.2", "4.2.8", "5.2.2", "6.2.9", "2.1.3", "2.2.9"]
source = "contract contracts/application.md#errors"

[resolution.9.67]
title = "Module accounts hold all venue custody"
contract = "The perps module account holds every uusdl of the perpetuals venue, including the balances of perps_fees and perps_insurance; the spot module account holds every spot denom, with book reserves, escrows and fee accruals kept as keeper records over that one balance."
applies_to = ["3.0.4", "3.1.3", "3.1.19", "4.1.4", "4.3.2"]
source = "contract contracts/perps.md#20-storage"

[resolution.9.68]
title = "The launchpad module account mints uusdl only at the USDL step"
contract = "The launchpad module account (modules/launchpad/keeper/keeper.go:40, modules/launchpad/types/keys.go:10) gains Minter permission for step 1 of MigrateV6120 and keeps no escrow for pool reserves; launchpad_treasury (modules/launchpad/types/keys.go:14) stays as it is."
applies_to = ["2.1.4", "2.2.16"]
source = "contract contracts/launchpad.md#5-quote-asset"

[resolution.9.69]
title = "Release work starts on the wired tree"
contract = "The baseline wiring task requires every domain completion task, and the release tasks require the wiring task, so the release candidate is built from a tree where every domain package set passed once."
applies_to = ["1.3.100", "8.4.1", "8.4.2", "8.4.10"]
source = "contract contracts/release.md#build-and-plan"

[capability_group.9.0]
title = "Resolution conformance"
children = ["9.0.1"]

[capability.9.0.1]
title = "Resolution conformance check"
reqs = ["9001.1", "9001.2", "9001.3", "9001.4", "9001.5", "9001.6", "9001.7", "9001.8", "9001.9", "9001.10", "9001.11", "9001.12", "9001.13", "9001.14", "9001.15", "9001.16", "9001.17", "9001.18", "9001.19", "9001.20", "9001.21", "9001.22", "9001.23", "9001.24", "9001.25", "9001.26", "9001.27", "9001.28", "9001.29", "9001.30", "9001.31", "9001.32", "9001.33", "9001.34", "9001.35", "9001.36", "9001.37", "9001.38", "9001.39", "9001.40", "9001.41", "9001.42", "9001.43", "9001.44", "9001.45", "9001.46", "9001.47", "9001.48", "9001.49", "9001.50", "9001.51", "9001.52", "9001.53", "9001.54", "9001.55", "9001.56", "9001.57", "9001.58", "9001.59", "9001.60", "9001.61", "9001.62", "9001.63", "9001.64", "9001.65", "9001.66", "9001.67", "9001.68", "9001.69", "9001.70", "9001.71", "9001.72", "9001.73", "9001.74", "9001.75", "9001.76", "9001.77", "9001.78", "9001.79", "9001.80", "9001.81", "9001.82", "9001.83", "9001.84", "9001.85", "9001.86", "9001.87", "9001.88", "9001.89", "9001.90", "9001.91", "9001.92", "9001.93", "9001.94", "9001.95", "9001.96", "9001.97", "9001.98"]
touches = ["tools/spec/check_resolutions.py", "tools/spec/check_resolutions_test.py"]
tests = ["tools/spec/check_resolutions_test.py"]
verification_contract = "python3 tools/spec/check_resolutions.py --feature release-v6-12-0"
do_1 = "Create tools/spec/check_resolutions.py with load(path) reading spec/<feature>/spec.kvx under the section, key and quoted-list rules of tools/specgen/kvx.go:45-84 (parse) and tools/specgen/kvx.go:228-244 (splitList), so a list value parses as the Go reader parses it."
do_2 = "Add known_ids(doc) returning the ids of every [task.*] and [capability.*] section, and resolve(ref, ids) that accepts an exact id or a wildcard <prefix>.* matching at least one id; the clause rule of tools/specgen/validate.go:132-148 stays as it is for the repository linter."
do_3 = "Add check(doc) that reports resolution.<id>: unknown <ref> for every unresolved applies_to id, resolution.<id>: applies to no task when none of its ids is a task, and decision.<N>: no resolution when no source equals decision D<N>, then exits 1 when any line was printed and 0 otherwise."
do_4 = "Accept --feature <slug> to pick spec/<slug>/spec.kvx in place of the active feature that tools/specgen/main.go:57 reads from workflow.kvx, and print one summary line resolutions <n> decisions <m> unresolved <k>."
do_5 = "Create tools/spec/check_resolutions_test.py with test_unknown_id_fails, test_wildcard_needs_a_match, test_decision_without_resolution_fails and test_release_feature_passes over small kvx strings and the real spec/release-v6-12-0/spec.kvx."

[acceptance.9.1.1]
feature = "9"
req = "9001.1"
scenario = "Given spec/release-v6-12-0/spec.kvx assembled with this feature, when python3 tools/spec/check_resolutions.py --feature release-v6-12-0 runs, then the source of resolution 9.1, 9.2, 9.3, 9.4 is \"decision D1\", every applies_to id (1.0.3, 1.0.4, 1.2.1, 1.2.3, 1.0.5, 8.4.1, 8.4.5, 8.4.14, 1.0.1) resolves to a task or capability of the spec, and no line decision.1: no resolution is printed."
contract = "contracts/release.md#build-and-plan"
test = "tools/spec/check_resolutions_test.py::test_decision_1_resolved (planned)"
qualification = "UNRUN"

